{"id": "De7N71Dxc-d", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Who is awake tonight? 🌕 On Sharad Purnima, Maa Lakshmi comes down at midnight and asks one question: \"Ko Jāgarti?\"\n\nTonight is Sharad Purnima, also called Kojagari Purnima. The name comes from Lakshmi's question: को जागर्ति? \"Ko jāgarti?\" means \"Who is awake?\"\n\nThe Nārada Purāṇa (ch. 124) describes this night. Lamps are lit after moonrise, kheer is kept in bowls in the bright moonlight, and the night is spent awake. At midnight, Mahalakshmi moves over the earth asking who is awake, and blesses the one who is awake and remembers her with wealth.\n\nAnd the moon? Tradition says tonight it shines with all 16 kalas. That's why so many homes are keeping kheer on the rooftop right now. 🍚✨\n\nYou're watching this, so you're awake. Answer her in the comments: JAI MAA LAKSHMI 🙏\n\n📚 Stay up tonight with a story: Rishi Katha Books 1–3 (Shailputri, Brahmacharini, Chandraghanta), set of 3 for ₹500 at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💛 Save this for next Sharad Purnima, and send it to the friend who's already asleep 😴\n\n#SharadPurnima #KojagariPurnima #SharadPurnima2026 #MaaLakshmi #Lakshmi #Kojagari #KheerUnderTheMoon #FullMoon #Purnima #HinduFestival #SanatanDharma #RishiKatha #KidsBooks", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792948455, "like_count": 20173, "comment_count": 808, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1796470088063840a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 56.666, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNELOaMDgaGbiJu5tdYfiEzQsTfQPgrpOidXjHFMo9ukU1OBfwVFgBRIAIEWYJsw2O6FudlBSi2FFCp5OdpXws-sQTMPkxST5TDyQ4.mp4?_nc_cat=106&_nc_oc=AdqIBs-RK9APOOaPF-5NASNzOOVl-pmoulqAhIc0CbdJuy8dC_SzxclrkxW0bY_cch3m-3ZWQqHDPlWG_XFeWTLd&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2